    <string name="privacy_body">All music files, lyrics, and covers are still stored on your local device. Network access is used to fetch lyrics and cover metadata, direct device-to-device transfers over the local network, and an optional Google Drive backup (off by default, only activates once you sign in and enable it) — which only backs up in-app data like favorites, play history, playlists, and EQ presets, stored in a private space under your own Google account that\'s invisible even to you in Drive\'s UI and accessible only by this app. Sensitive fields such as your NetEase Cloud Music cookie and LAN device IP are encrypted before upload, never stored in plain text in the cloud.</string>
